# Main Branch Protection Workflow

- Do not make code changes directly on `main` or `master`.
- Before editing code, check the current branch. If it is `main` or `master`, create or switch to a feature branch first.
- Do not commit or push directly to `main` or `master`.
- All changes intended for `main` must go through a pull request.
- Merge to `main` only after required CI checks pass.
- If a task explicitly requires an emergency hotfix on `main`, ask for user confirmation before making changes.

```bash
# Good workflow
git switch -c feature/<short-description>
# make changes, commit, push, open PR
# merge only after CI passes
```
